dsv41 patch 0045 (19.10.2026): the TP all-gathers of a decode round over the plugin's RDMA ring instead of NCCL.
Base: the recipe's plugin vllm_exl3_moe (cc59c36): rdma.py and csrc/exl3_rdma.cu as in the image.
Why: rdma.py moves only CudaCommunicator.all_reduce to the ring, so each decode round still made ~10 NCCL calls: the
DSpark drafter's Markov pairs (5 per round, [R, 2] fp32, in the drafter graph), the Engram rows of layers 1 and 14
([R, 12, 256] bf16, in the target graph) and the logits (eager, [R, 64640] bf16: 776 KB at 6 rows, 3.1 MB at 24).
Back to back NCCL takes 35.9 us per call against 14.6 us on the ring ([6, 5120] in a graph, recipe FINDINGS.md no. 11).
Inside a graph each NCCL call also goes through a host node and NCCL's proxy thread, which waits on a condition
variable whenever no NCCL op is pending (NCCL src/proxy.cc), i.e. between these calls. TensorFold sends every decode
gather up to 4.25 MB over RDMA.
How: exl3_rdma.cu: stage_kernel templated on the copy unit (uint4 for the all-reduce = the old code; uint32_t for
gathers whose rows are not a multiple of 16 bytes, e.g. one Markov pair = 8 bytes); a new gather_kernel (waits on the
flags like sum_kernel, both flag modes, then copies all ranks as [outer][world][inner] = torch.cat along dim) and the
binding all_gather(h, x, out, outer). Ring, sequence counter, proxy and slots are shared: all-reduces and all-gathers
use one sequence, and both ranks issue them in the same order (same model code; none of the redirected gathers runs on
a side stream). rdma.py: EXL3_RDMA_AG=1 also patches CudaCommunicator.all_gather; the path depends only on dtype, shape
and dim (equal on all ranks), misalignment is fixed locally with a copy. Slot size = max(all-reduce, all-gather limit);
the all-reduce limit stays EXL3_RDMA_AR_MAX_KB (prefill all-reduces stay on NCCL). Gathers above the limit (prefill
Engram, vision) and other groups stay on NCCL; if a rank fails to set up the ring, both ranks fall back to NCCL.
Exact: a pure copy, the same bytes as NCCL all_gather + movedim/reshape on both ranks.
Measured (GB10, 2000 MHz): two-node test passed (bits against NCCL for all decode shapes, a round graph with
interleaved all-reduces, 200 repetitions, both flag modes, latency after pauses). Serve with 0046 against the same image
without switches: 1 stream +1.6 %, geometric mean over all T = 1 cells (prose / code / JSON, 1 / 3 / 4 streams) +1.0 %.
Switch: EXL3_RDMA_AG=1 (default 0 = previous behaviour), EXL3_RDMA_AG_MAX_KB (default 256: Markov pairs and Engram rows;
3072: also the logits up to 24 rows, which we use). Pinned host memory per rank: 3 MB at 256 KB, 36 MB at 3072 KB.
JIT: new source hash; build it before the first start: python3 -c 'from vllm_exl3_moe import rdma; rdma.ext()'.

